          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are women's protein shakes a waste of money?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Often, yes. Many deliver 15-20 g of protein per scoop, replace some of it with collagen, add biotin or botanicals in small amounts, and cost more per gram of protein than plain whey. A few are decent powders with a different label. Judge them on protein per serving, cost per 25 g of protein and certification."
